headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

docs {
  WhatsApp-style rooms on Django-Bolt + Sockudo.

  Open this folder in Bruno (Open Collection).
  Select environment: local
  Django must be running: http://127.0.0.1:8000

  Suggested order:
  1. Users → List users (copy two ids into env userId / otherUserId)
  2. Chat → Create direct room or Create group room (saves roomId)
  3. Chat → List rooms (unread + total_unread)
  4. Chat → Send message as userId (saves messageId)
  5. Chat → List rooms as otherUserId (unread should rise)
  6. Chat → Mark delivered as otherUserId
  7. Chat → Mark room read as otherUserId (unread 0, read ticks)

  Live bubbles need Sockudo + chat.html. These requests test HTTP only.

  unread = messages after RoomMember.last_read_at, excluding my own.
  delivered/read = MessageReceipt rows per recipient (ticks), not the badge.
}
